## rust-codex-compiler back on master

Steve's call: fast-forward `master` to `zonk-and-default`, `77bd70b` ->
`ee9cb16`, pushed. That is 35 commits: 5 type-engine commits up to the park
point `9044a29`, then 30 rocemit/Mem commits (a new `roc_emit.rs`, plus about
170 lines in shared files including `irdump.rs`, `ir.rs`, `desugar.rs` and
`lowering.rs`). Every release binary in `~/build/rust-target/release`
predated commits to its own sources, so they are rebuilt from master before
any consumer arm runs.

    cargo build --release   at ee9cb16, 2m08s, exit 0
    cargo test              did NOT compile: c6792a2 gave roc_emit's num_lit
                            an f32 flag and left three unit tests calling it
                            with one argument. The fix passes `false`, the
                            f64 path those tests are about. 243 passed,
                            0 failed.

The fix is confined to `#[cfg(test)]`, so the release binaries built from
`ee9cb16` are the ones the consumer arms use.

**The Rust front end's resolver falls back to CODEX_ROOT** (cobblestone-qemu
`FINDINGS.md` 3, third row). Every unit in the three dirs carries ListUtils and
Tuple, and the Rust-side arms run with `CODEX_ROOT` unset, so a missing cite
refuses instead of resolving against the ambient checkout.

## Consumers without tracked writes: all green

    safari spec/run.sh   54 specs pass, grading at least 2,351 values
    run-interp           cobblestone 28/28 · roc 46/46 · safari 54/54 match
    ir-rust              cobblestone 28/28 · roc 46/46 · safari 54/54 agree
    ir-zig               cobblestone 28/28 · roc 46/46 · safari 54/54 match
    run-zig (earlier)    cobblestone 28/28 · roc 44 + 2 filed · safari 54/54

The Rust arms used `~/build/rust-target/release`, built from master `ee9cb16`,
and `ir-zig` used `zigemit 9fff850c`. `ir-rust` agreeing everywhere means the 35
commits master took change nothing `irdump` emits for these 128 units.

**CODEX_ROOT, eliminated at its source (Steve).** The Rust tools read it in two
places: the `bundle` binary, and `bundle::load`'s lazy fallback for a unit that
lacks a chapter. `~/.bashrc` line 4 exported it globally at NewRepository, so the
fallback would have landed there silently. Line 4 is deleted. Every live script
names its checkout or refuses without one; the transpilers use
`COBBLESTONE_ROOT`, and only the deprecated ladder could have relied on the
global.

**Direction, not yet done:** "we should have Rust totally do its own resolution
going forward. All these fallthroughs just make the code more fragile and harder
to reason about." The fallback and `CODEXC_RAW` are debt. The replacement, and
how it names its checkout, are to be designed with Steve before coding.

